SUMMARY:Hairspray
DESCRIPTION:It’s 1962 in Baltimore\, and the lovable plus-size teen\, Tracy Turnblad\, has only one desire – to dance on the popular “Corny Collins Show.” When her dream comes true\, Tracy is transformed from social outcast to sudden star. She must use her newfound power to dethrone the reigning Teen Queen\, win the affections of heartthrob\, Link Larkin\, and integrate a TV network… all without denting her ‘do! Hairspray\, winner of eight Tony Awards\, including Best Musical\, is a family-friendly musical\, piled bouffant-high with laughter\, romance and deliriously tuneful songs. \nBook by Mark O’Donnell & Thomas Meehan \nMusic by Marc Shaiman \nLyrics by Scott Wittman & Marc Shaiman \nBased on the New Line Cinema film\, written and directed by John Waters
URL:https://unitedarts.org/calendar/hairspray/2026-09-18/
LOCATION:Raleigh Little Theatre\, 301 Pogue St\, Raleigh\, 27607
ORGANIZER;CN="Raleigh Little Theatre":MAILTO:boxoffice@raleighlittletheatre.org
END:VEVENT
